  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math> represents the equation of state of some gases. Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is the pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is the volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is the temperature and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are the constants. The physical quantity, which has dimensional formula as that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;, will be :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TgqG5",
      "text": "Bulk modulus",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vxw8u",
      "text": "Modulus of rigidity",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iqgRg",
      "text": "Compressibility",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32YnP",
      "text": "Energy density",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to the principle of dimensional homogeneity, the dimensions of each &nbsp;terms of a dimensional equation on both sides are the same.</p><p>So,&nbsp;dimension of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;will be same,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>V</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>And dimension of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be same,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>P</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>From above two relations, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>P</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>P</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;is the dimension of compressibility.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
